<!--
  ILS approaches for Saint Andrews (EGSAN) — runway 13 / 31
  Source airport XML: PackageSources\Scenery\airport-eg56-saint-andrews\scenery\EG56.xml

  HOW TO USE
  ----------
  1. Copy everything between PASTE START and PASTE END.
  2. Paste it inside the <Airport> element in EG56.xml, just before </Airport>
     (after the apron / painted-element / edge-light blocks is fine).
  3. Also fix the two existing <Ils> blocks (see ILS FIXES below).
     Your current GlideSlope pitch is 0.0, which will not give a 3° path,
     and there is no <Dme /> child even though DME is required for this
     procedure to make sense in the GPS / FMS.
  4. Rebuild the package in Dev Mode, then confirm the procedures appear
     as ILS 13 and ILS 31 in the world map / MCDU.

  GEOMETRY USED
  -------------
  Runway 13/31, true heading 130 / 310, magvar 0
  Threshold 13 : 56.30934030  -2.75580025
  Threshold 31 : 56.29933946  -2.73431604
  Field elev   : ~272 ft (82.86 m)
  3° GS        : ~318 ft per NM, plus 50 ft TCH

  IAF  = 10.0 NM on the extended centreline, 2000 ft
  FAF  =  5.0 NM on the extended centreline, 1900 ft  (GS intercept)
  MAP  = runway threshold
  Hold = 10 NM past the far threshold, 3000 ft

  Region EG is the UK ICAO prefix used for terminal waypoints.
-->

